Two defects, both mine.

1. The picker listed one row per parallel configuration, so a handful of models
   became 25 rows of `Qwen3-4B-FP8@dp2`, `@dp4`, ... That is the shape the
   variant ids have on the wire, but it is not what a person is choosing: they
   pick a model, then how it is served. openaiModelDiscovery now collapses
   variants to one row per model and records the full id list; the picker's
   dp/pp row reads that list and the choice is composed back into
   `base@dpN@ppM` at selection time. 25 rows → 11.

2. Descriptions still read "Discovered from OpenAI-compatible endpoint". The
   backend-description lookup had been added to bootstrap.ts, which is a
   different discovery path than the one this setup actually uses. Moved the
   helper into npuVariants and applied it where the options are really built.

dp/pp is now session state rather than part of the focused value, so moving
between models no longer rewrites the selection, and a configuration the backend
never advertised is never composed.

