From f67bfeb8b414af23f564216285b953325b3991b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:11:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] model picker: apply NPU collapsing and descriptions on
 the cached path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous fix only ran during model discovery, but the picker normally
renders from the cached option list — it even says so ("Local OpenAI-compatible
models are up to date"). So a stale cache kept showing one row per dp/pp
combination with the generic "Discovered from ..." description, and the fix
looked like it had done nothing.

Collapse variants and apply backend descriptions where the option list is
assembled, which covers both the fresh and cached paths.

getDiscoveredModelIds() now falls back to the backend description map's keys.
Discovery may never run in a session, and without that fallback the dp/pp
selector had no configurations to offer whenever the list came from cache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
